cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mythoscope, please cite it."
title: "Mythoscope: a computational framework for comparative mythology"
abstract: >-
  Mythoscope builds a corpus of myth and folklore texts, embeds them into an
  explorable semantic space, extracts character/place/time graphs, and assembles
  a cross-linked motif database integrating the Thompson (TMI), Aarne–Thompson–Uther
  (ATU), and Berezkin indexes.
type: software
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
url: "https://mythoscope.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/mythoscope"
keywords:
  - computational folkloristics
  - comparative mythology
  - digital humanities
  - motif index
  - cultural evolution
authors:
  - given-names: "FIRST"
    family-names: "LAST"
